{"seq":1,"mint":"C7","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":false,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"`ExtentEntry` already carries four `#[serde(default)]` fields whose absence is documented as \"not recorded\" rather than as a default value — `world_root`, `kind`, `out_len` and `matcher`","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F4","F23"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"/// `world_root` is `#[serde(default)]` for entries minted before it\n/// existed. An empty root is not \"unknown repository\" — it marks a state\n/// that was resolved from the process's working directory rather than\n/// from what the observation touched, and is therefore comparable with\n/// nothing. `check` treats it that way rather than guessing.","why":"The captured documentation says an absent/default `world_root` is an empty root with a specific working-directory meaning, not “not recorded”.","quoted":true}],"at":1790112507,"cost":0.00286874,"elapsed_ms":20193,"attempts":2,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0}
